From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ghostframe <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:23:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] v4l2: let the caller name the video device

`enumerate_devices` returns the first /dev/videoN that has an output mplane
queue and a matching media device, with no check that the device decodes
anything. On an RK3399 that is the hantro *encoder*, and H.264 decode fails
with `Unrecoverable decoding error` even though rkvdec on another node
handles the same stream. Node numbering is not stable across boots either,
so the right node cannot simply be written down once.

`C2V4L2DecoderOptions::video_device_path` already existed for this, carrying
`TODO: This is currently unused, but we should plumb it to V4L2Device
initialization`. This is that plumbing:

  V4l2Device::new_with_device_path
  V4l2StatelessDecoderBackend::new_with_device_path
  StatelessDecoder::<Codec, _>::new_v4l2_with_device_path   (av1/h264/vp8/vp9)

`None` keeps the scanning behaviour, so `new()`/`new_v4l2()` are unchanged
for every existing caller. `C2V4L2Decoder` now carries the option through
rather than dropping it.
